 🚢 Good Tuesday afternoon. We take a moment to remember, on this date in 1975, the sinking of the Great Lakes iron-ore freighter Edmund Fitzgerald in a storm on Lake Superior. The entire crew of 29 perished. Read more . 

 Today's newsletter, edited by Alex Fitzpatrick, is 683 words, a 2½-min. read. Thanks to Sheryl Miller for copy editing . 🏛️ Breaking: House Republicans elected Judiciary Chair Jim Jordan (R-Ohio) as their new leader, handing the reins of the battered GOP conference to one of its most prominent conservative firebrands. Rep. Steve Scalise (R-La.) trailed Jordan by 33 votes in a secret ballot, 106-73 . Go deeper . 

 ⚡️ Situational awareness: Caleb Orr will become White House deputy chief of staff for policy, succeeding Stephen Miller, Axios' Alex Isenstadt reports . Orr previously was an adviser in Miller's policy office.

 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 1 big thing: Hegseth comes out swinging 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth holds a press conference at the Pentagon today. Photo: Nathan Howard/AP Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth lambasted Rep. Thomas Massie's (R-Ky.) push to oust him today, Axios' Avery Lotz reports. 

 Massie introduced articles of impeachment against Hegseth yesterday over his handling of the Iran war and other alleged misconduct. 🎤 Hegseth told reporters at the Pentagon this morning: "They impeached President Trump over a perfect phone call. They impeached him again in his final week in office," referencing Trump's first impeachment over a phone call in which he pressed Ukraine to investigate Joe Biden and his second over the Jan. 6 attack.

 "Both times, he came back stronger, and the American people sent him back to the White House. Now they're trying a third time. This time against a member of his Cabinet." "They will fail again, and if standing with President Trump puts me in that company, I'll take that company every day of the week." 🪖 Hegseth also defended controversial U.S. military operations in Iran, Venezuela and the Caribbean.

 "We sank the boats carrying poison into our communities. We put a narco dictator in handcuffs. These are not high crimes. This is the job, and it's the job well done." President Trump gave Hegseth's performance "an 'A' PLUS, PLUS, PLUS" in a Truth Social post . 

 Go deeper . 
 
