 2. 📜 MLK draft could fetch $10M 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photo: Tony Cenicola/The New York Times A handwritten draft of Martin Luther King Jr.'s "I Have a Dream" speech is going up for auction in January at Christie's.

 The document, found in a desk drawer of a former aide, is expected to sell for more than $10 million. The proceeds will go toward the King Center and other philanthropic causes.

 Photo: Christie's ✍️ The seven pages of yellow legal pad paper are believed to be the only surviving handwritten version of King's final draft.

 Peter Klarnet, Christie's manuscript specialist, told The New York Times: "This is the most important manuscript I've ever had the honor to handle." Gift link ... Auction details . 

 
 
