 4. ✈️ 1 for the road: Dulles sneak peek 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The new United Club at Dulles Concourse E. Image: United Airlines Dulles Airport's new Concourse E opens today, bringing United Airlines travelers spacious gates, more concessions and a swanky club lounge, Axios D.C.'s Cuneyt Dil reports after getting a sneak peek yesterday. 

 The project is one step toward Dulles' massive modernization, which will take up to 10 years, phase out "people movers" and add more gates. 🍽️ At yesterday's unveiling, the sleek aesthetics and new food options (we heard one person rave about Bonchon Korean Fried Chicken) got plenty of attention. 

 So did the bathrooms. Photo: Cuneyt Dil/Axios 🚇 The new United Club lounge has a local nod: The escalator entrance pays homage to the Metro's iconic brutalist stations.

 Inside, there are two buffet stations, a bar and seating for more than 600 customers. Go deeper . 

 
 
